#:culture{:id "rus.craft.matryoshka-doll", :name "Matryoshka doll", :country "RUS", :kind :craft, :summary "The first Russian nested doll set was carved in the 1890s by craftsman Vasily Zvyozdochkin from a design by folk painter Sergey Malyutin, and the dolls continue to be mass-produced as a traditional handicraft to this day.", :url "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matryoshka_doll", :url-provenance :wikipedia-en, :retrieved-at "2026-07-17"}
